WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.360
All four budget answers
named Roborock.

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:04.960
Each named a different
Roborock model first.

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:07.160
Same under-$500 prompt.

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:09.660
Same two-story home
and long-haired cat.

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:12.960
ChatGPT led with the Q10 X5+.

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:15.820
Claude picked the Q7 M5+.

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:18.100
Gemini named the Qrevo S first.

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:21.960
Perplexity named the Q10 S5+
alongside a Yeedi.

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:25.800
Roborock also ranked first
in all four brand comparisons.

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:27.980
That’s agreement at the brand level.

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:31.080
The budget answers tell you
which products actually came up.

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:33.920
We didn’t verify prices
or test the vacuums.

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:35.340
Try this for your brand.

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:37.040
Run one shopper question.

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:38.700
Record the exact model,

00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:41.260
why the assistant brought it up,
and any caveat.

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:44.360
Then check if that’s the product
you want shoppers to find.

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:47.360
Explore benchmark at
getrecoscope.com.
